        <section><h3>Examples</h3>
            <p class="${"examples"}">Let ${escape(`\\(A = \\{1, 2\\}\\)`)} and ${escape(`\\(B = \\{2, 3, 4\\}\\)`)}, then ${escape(`\\(A\\cap B = \\{2\\}\\)`)}</p>
            <p class="${"examples"}">Let ${escape(`\\(A = \\{1, 2\\}\\)`)} and ${escape(`\\(B = \\{3, 4\\}\\)`)}, then ${escape(`\\(A\\cap B = \\phi\\)`)}</p></section>
        <section><h3>Some properties of the Operation of Union</h3>
            <ol><li>\\(A\\cap B = B\\cap A\\) (Commutative law)</li>
                <li>\\((A\\cap B)\\cap C = A\\cap (B\\cap C)\\) (Associative law)</li>
                <li>\\(A\\cap \\phi = \\phi\\) (Law of identity element)</li>
                <li>\\(A\\cap A = A\\) (Idempotent law)</li>
                <li>\\(U\\cup A = U\\) (Law of U)</li>
                <li>\\(A\\cap (B\\cup C) = (A\\cap B)\\cup (A\\cap C)\\) (Distributive law)</li></ol></section>
        <section><h2>Difference of sets</h2>
            <div class="${"definition"}"><p>The difference of two sets \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) is the set \\(C\\) which consists of all those elements which are in \\(A\\) but not in \\(B\\). ${escape(`\\[A- B = \\{x:x\\in A ~and~x\\notin B\\}\\]`)}</p></div>
